{"skill":{"slug":"x-ai","displayName":"xAI / Grok"},"version":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1771690964816,"changelog":"- Added a prominent link to external installation and use instructions at the top of the setup section.\n- No changes to functionality or commands; documentation update only.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":".gitignore","size":25,"sha256":"4ad2dd72b5b8511335b75e7b4dac1a8c92c576a7735f1e275b58c26ef1a1bef2","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"package.json","size":312,"sha256":"3c2cf2d4435cc342084cfcefd0fb6cfb98357dd0df0498aad23c663940500b5f","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"README.md","size":1462,"sha256":"ff598eee99aab8829b4c28a7ed204cc937abe6185ad951b553b7a43487456aff","contentType":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2886,"sha256":"3308a38966c33a1235af54e7b59627061cdb36b00aa4d79f831f667edf010ff6","contentType":null},{"path":"scripts/chat.js","size":6278,"sha256":"48d61df69daebb5f75c3f22e04a39cf3df4c86597d0154d46ad239fa149fdb23","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/models.js","size":1803,"sha256":"ed8c8592703dded8479734260757c2e17c3faf9697015a3fc9dc0d551b98fee8","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/search-x.js","size":6856,"sha256":"a915a0f3bfcc2fb948306d53ba5c99958633b85f22d1605e4903a5100d8e6ac3","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2110,"sha256":"97484edb535143be064395e58ed4c45fcb11db68fd2caba17f713a1a4e656e4c","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789075433183,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2245ee03eeb244934db0efd58a926c64c6a502cb9b486c03845dad63c9801bb6","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2245ee03eeb244934db0efd58a926c64c6a502cb9b486c03845dad63c9801bb6","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: x-ai\nVersion: 1.0.2\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to a potential arbitrary file read vulnerability in `scripts/chat.js`. The `imageToBase64` function uses `path.resolve` and `fs.readFileSync` on a user-provided image path. While it includes an extension whitelist (e.g., `.jpg`, `.png`), an attacker could potentially craft a path (e.g., `../../../secrets/mykey.png`) to read sensitive files that happen to have an allowed image extension and are accessible via path traversal. This is a vulnerability, not clear malicious intent, as the code's purpose is to facilitate image uploads to the xAI API. No evidence of prompt injection or other malicious behavior was found.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779165772407},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":13,"checkedAt":1789075433183},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This appears to be a real xAI/Grok integration, but it needs review because image uploads can transmit unintended local files and one documented install path is not pinned to an audited version.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of XAI_API_KEY and network access to api.x.ai is expected, but prompts and image/file contents are sent to a third-party API without point-of-use confirmation or robust file validation.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"There are no install hooks or package dependencies, but the README documents an alternate git clone from a mutable GitHub default branch rather than an audited commit or signed release.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill is user-invocable and says model-autonomous invocation is disabled; broad natural-language examples and the 'ask grok' trigger could still route prompts or images to an external API if users do not realize the skill is being invoked.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, background workers, scheduled tasks, privilege escalation, writes, or credential stores beyond the XAI_API_KEY environment variable were found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The chat, model-listing, vision, and X search scripts are coherent with an xAI integration, but the vision path reads and uploads a user-supplied local path using only extension checks, which conflicts with the claim that it does not read arbitrary local files.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only from the reviewed ClawHub package or a pinned commit. Treat every prompt and image as being sent to xAI, avoid secrets or regulated data, and do not use the image option on symlinks, renamed non-images, or files you have not personally selected.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The .env entry is a normal ignore pattern for an API-key based project, not evidence that the skill reads credential files.\n[TP4] expected: The inspected package includes chat.js, models.js, and search-x.js; model listing and X search are documented in SKILL.md and fit the xAI integration purpose.\n[AE1] expected: The referenced scripts were present locally and fully inspected, so the partial-inspection concern is not supported for this adjudication.\n[AR2] expected: The cited text is a CLI option that suppresses a missing-citation warning, not a safety or ethics anti-refusal instruction.\n[SQP-2] expected: External transmission of prompts and images is core to the skill and is disclosed in SKILL.md, but README/help text and runtime behavior could make that clearer before upload.\n[SQP-1] expected: The natural-language examples explicitly name Grok, but they are broad enough that users should understand invocation sends content to xAI.\n[LP3] expected: XAI_API_KEY access is necessary for the xAI API; the metadata declares the env requirement, though a stricter permission declaration would improve clarity.\n[TR2] expected: The trigger includes 'ask grok', which is explicit about Grok but could still overlap with ordinary assistant phrasing.\n[SDI-1] expected: X/Twitter search is specifically documented in SKILL.md as a bundled script, although README.md does not mention it.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted as a material concern: chat.js accepts image uploads by extension only, follows symlinks, has no regular-file or size checks, and then sends the bytes to api.x.ai.\n[T08] unexpected: Accepted as an install hygiene concern: the README's direct git clone alternative can install future unaudited repository contents.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789075433183}}}}}